From: pear <pear@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Sep 2001 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [model, perf] feat: Qwen3.5's packed short convolution in one
 FLA kernel launch

For packed sequences the Gated DeltaNet's short convolution is one call of FLA's Triton causal_conv1d over
cu_seqlens instead of an nn.Conv1d per sequence, with SiLU applied to its output. The context-parallel halo is
assembled token-major, and FLA's convolution autotuners no longer re-tune for every packed length.
---
